[{:db/id "q-49908/selection/25f2b653d67e901ed8f3a5b197ba86f45d2783a4eb50a9d8395befd1e30401a5" :answer/id #uuid "d4635e99-37ab-53ed-a275-dadd0a021879" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|3x+1|+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49908/selection/952c6ebf611ebbccd59ff00440767d9a22ed200e3cc92071385a285613cd9fce" :answer/id #uuid "db292bc9-5f84-511e-9051-a0b1f3d7a6de" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|-3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|3x+1|+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49908/selection/bbc5c4be97784f9402d22eb10aff8a8300f58b2c4fafe8d183b3f342fad6bdfd" :answer/id #uuid "23e70970-9b4c-56da-b14d-9fc32a8cbdd0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|3x+1|+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49908/selection/97f965fe18176d176c63a04a4a986d985497b8edd4aa33e6c57726c93e3e7b98" :answer/id #uuid "9e75d514-6353-5579-8d7e-665dc82b2915" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+\\operatorname{ln}⁡|3x+1|+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49908/selection/a94432c356a2dd558892292d8c3936df9f877657cc53af30ec866f63bfab8cbe" :answer/id #uuid "519743e3-cd0c-557d-b755-5ccabca252cf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|3x+1|+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49908/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "0ddb7940-089d-513e-85e6-afc05b16a677" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-49908/selection/a94432c356a2dd558892292d8c3936df9f877657cc53af30ec866f63bfab8cbe" :answer-field/choices ["q-49908/selection/25f2b653d67e901ed8f3a5b197ba86f45d2783a4eb50a9d8395befd1e30401a5" "q-49908/selection/952c6ebf611ebbccd59ff00440767d9a22ed200e3cc92071385a285613cd9fce" "q-49908/selection/bbc5c4be97784f9402d22eb10aff8a8300f58b2c4fafe8d183b3f342fad6bdfd" "q-49908/selection/97f965fe18176d176c63a04a4a986d985497b8edd4aa33e6c57726c93e3e7b98" "q-49908/selection/a94432c356a2dd558892292d8c3936df9f877657cc53af30ec866f63bfab8cbe"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-49908" :question/id #uuid "9762f314-b655-58a9-a815-41bc2f93077e" :question/math-academy-id "q-49908" :question/problem "$\\int \\frac{2}{3{x}^{2}+x}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we note that the denominator of the integrand can be factored as\n\n$$\n3{x}^{2}+x=x(3x+1).\n$$\n\nWe convert the integrand into a sum of partial fractions:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{x(3x+1)} & =\\frac{A}{x}+\\frac{B}{(3x+1)},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n2=A(3x+1)+Bx.\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=-\\frac{1}{3},$ we can eliminate $A$ and solve for $B:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2 & =A(3(-\\frac{1}{3})+1)+B(-\\frac{1}{3}) \\\\ 2 & =-\\frac{1}{3}B \\\\ 6 & =-B \\\\ B & =-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, plugging in $x=0,$ we can eliminate $B$ and solve for $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2 & =A(3(0)+1)+B(0) \\\\ 2 & =A\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{x(3x+1)}=\\frac{2}{x}-\\frac{6}{3x+1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{2}{x(3x+1)}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{2}{x}-\\frac{6}{3x+1})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x-2\\int \\frac{3}{3x+1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|3x+1|+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-49908/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d54bab77-d77f-5275-b454-ddb565eaa280"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-49908"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-348933/field-1/7dd401d47aa00849c11dc6c2796da32bd75f75d08745e7898f8a772573778229" :answer/id #uuid "d7cb62f1-624b-5572-8b9d-2e57dd7cb8d8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{11}{9}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-348933/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "102cb884-e241-59e7-8d95-bc521e1d32c3" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-348933/field-1/7dd401d47aa00849c11dc6c2796da32bd75f75d08745e7898f8a772573778229" :answer-field/choices ["q-348933/field-1/7dd401d47aa00849c11dc6c2796da32bd75f75d08745e7898f8a772573778229"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-348933/field-2/84b25bb5d8e66cd3720fba0782c29531516ad0cd6b15dc0856177aac0ff562df" :answer/id #uuid "07099bbf-40db-554d-af1a-de896fb2e589" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{11}{9}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-348933/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "522f3f76-4d45-55c6-9c0d-f0605d17a519" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-348933/field-2/84b25bb5d8e66cd3720fba0782c29531516ad0cd6b15dc0856177aac0ff562df" :answer-field/choices ["q-348933/field-2/84b25bb5d8e66cd3720fba0782c29531516ad0cd6b15dc0856177aac0ff562df"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-348933" :question/id #uuid "16dae2d4-d8c2-58dc-951e-8924c446f8fe" :question/math-academy-id "q-348933" :question/problem "Evaluate the following indefinite integral and fill in the missing coefficients.\n\n$\\int \\frac{11}{(2x+5)(x-2)}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}$\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2x+5|\\,+\\,$\n{{field-2}}$\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-2|+C$" :question/worked-solution "First, we note that the denominator of the integrand can be factored as\n\n$$\n(2x+5)(x-2).\n$$\n\nWe convert the integrand into a sum of partial fractions:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{11}{(2x+5)(x-2)} & =\\frac{A}{2x+5}+\\frac{B}{x-2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n11=A(x-2)+B(2x+5).\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=2,$ we can eliminate $A$ and solve for $B:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}11 & =9B \\\\ B & =\\frac{11}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, plugging in $x=-\\frac{5}{2},$ we can eliminate $B$ and solve for $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}11 & =-\\frac{9}{2}A \\\\ A & =-\\frac{22}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{11}{(2x+5)(x-2)}=-\\frac{22}{9(2x+5)}+\\frac{11}{9(x-2)}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{11}{(2x+5)(x-2)}\\,\\text{d}x & =-\\frac{22}{9}\\int \\frac{1}{2x+5}\\,\\text{d}x+\\frac{11}{9}\\int \\frac{1}{x-2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{11}{9}\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2x+5|+\\frac{11}{9}\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-2|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-348933/field-1" "q-348933/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d54bab77-d77f-5275-b454-ddb565eaa280"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-348933"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-348898/field-1/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer/id #uuid "9313535f-7431-5830-bd3d-58895013ec28" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-348898/field-1/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "f9c952b5-b0b8-5452-8c02-cc50c1112f68" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-348898/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "19e6f951-0205-55ba-824c-bc46c458c916" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-348898/field-1/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer-field/choices ["q-348898/field-1/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" "q-348898/field-1/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-348898/field-2/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "b34bcff9-df4c-5706-87b3-081d015c2a81" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-348898/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "08ee7f52-3d9e-53df-8993-e91d3408c9c2" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-348898/field-2/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer-field/choices ["q-348898/field-2/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-348898" :question/id #uuid "a3ce1874-816d-5616-9c10-d203d3f4b0a6" :question/math-academy-id "q-348898" :question/problem "Evaluate the following indefinite integral and fill in the missing coefficients.\n\n$\\int \\frac{7x-11}{(x-8)(x+1)}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}$\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-8|\\,+\\,$\n{{field-2}}$\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+1|+C$" :question/worked-solution "First, we note that the denominator of the integrand can be factored as\n\n$$\n(x-8)(x+1).\n$$\n\nWe convert the integrand into a sum of partial fractions:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{7x-11}{(x-8)(x+1)} & =\\frac{A}{x-8}+\\frac{B}{x+1},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n7x-11=A(x+1)+B(x-8).\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=8,$ we can eliminate $B$ and solve for $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7(8)-11 & =A(8+1)+B(8-8) \\\\ 45 & =9A \\\\ A & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, plugging in $x=-1,$ we can eliminate $A$ and solve for $B:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7(-1)-11 & =A(-1+1)+B(-1-8) \\\\ -18 & =-9B \\\\ B & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{7x-11}{(x-8)(x+1)}=\\frac{5}{x-8}+\\frac{2}{x+1}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{7x-11}{(x-8)(x+1)}\\,\\text{d}x & =5\\int \\frac{1}{x-8}\\,\\text{d}x+2\\int \\frac{1}{x+1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =5\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-8|+2\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+1|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-348898/field-1" "q-348898/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d54bab77-d77f-5275-b454-ddb565eaa280"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-348898"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-49905/selection/04ab8c59d12921ca2d995f79fd8be713086563c65c468afaa0d4bd8ea5bfffaf" :answer/id #uuid "823fef91-4b8a-517d-85f7-21e44fa5231b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{7}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49905/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "42d05105-e872-579a-8c3b-8025f05506eb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49905/selection/c087f5dc559272d193745a4428553203b94404f681d8529e6e619348c0528d10" :answer/id #uuid "cad5fd07-0ca0-5bc8-a23e-dca48f4c0370" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49905/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" :answer/id #uuid "94aff6cc-ad04-5afb-ba0a-51dbb7925846" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49905/selection/4280bcd0914e40dbdc039bc97ee5d5baafd2654e75e9b692316d9c28c4842856" :answer/id #uuid "4ddcd1b4-11fa-575f-bd1d-9ee3213f0953" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49905/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "4239dd8c-1ffc-52b1-9e7b-8119073af6c6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-49905/selection/4280bcd0914e40dbdc039bc97ee5d5baafd2654e75e9b692316d9c28c4842856" :answer-field/choices ["q-49905/selection/04ab8c59d12921ca2d995f79fd8be713086563c65c468afaa0d4bd8ea5bfffaf" "q-49905/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-49905/selection/c087f5dc559272d193745a4428553203b94404f681d8529e6e619348c0528d10" "q-49905/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" "q-49905/selection/4280bcd0914e40dbdc039bc97ee5d5baafd2654e75e9b692316d9c28c4842856"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-49905" :question/id #uuid "220a8b03-1c32-5c37-9106-3fe4303bad77" :question/math-academy-id "q-49905" :question/problem "Given that\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{5x-1}{(x-3)(2x+1)}\\,\\text{d}x=a\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-3|+b\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2x+1|+C,\n$$\n\nfind the value of $a+b.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we convert the integrand into a sum of partial fractions:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5x-1}{(x-3)(2x+1)} & =\\frac{A}{x-3}+\\frac{B}{2x+1},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n5x-1=A(2x+1)+B(x-3).\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=-\\frac{1}{2},$ we can eliminate $A$ and solve for $B:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5(-\\frac{1}{2})-1 & =A(2(-\\frac{1}{2})+1)+B(-\\frac{1}{2}-3) \\\\ -\\frac{7}{2} & =-\\frac{7}{2}B \\\\ B & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, plugging in $x=3,$ we can eliminate $B$ and solve for $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5(3)-1 & =A(2(3)+1)+B(3-3) \\\\ 14 & =7A \\\\ A & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5x-1}{(x-3)(2x+1)}=\\frac{2}{x-3}+\\frac{1}{2x+1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{5x-1}{(x-3)(2x+1)}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{2}{x-3}+\\frac{1}{2x+1})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\int \\frac{1}{x-3}\\,\\text{d}x+\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\frac{2}{2x+1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-3|+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2x+1|+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, $a=2,b=\\frac{1}{2},$ and $a+b=2+\\frac{1}{2}=\\frac{5}{2}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-49905/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d54bab77-d77f-5275-b454-ddb565eaa280"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-49905"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-348976/field-1/43082b8da21cdc54a702621d76d39594581d5e4d848fd6a50a0a3d4ef85e5bb6" :answer/id #uuid "483f7011-c7aa-512d-87b8-a19f9958a524" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{11}{3}\\ln(5)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-348976/field-1/9d25723a5db975934b4a4f87336359c9306e6e88d4ce71608f50b86c88284c1b" :answer/id #uuid "460331c6-d06c-57b0-8fd2-3ca938fc55fb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\ln(5)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-348976/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "26f01bd9-0772-5dd9-979c-19468dbb5bd4" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-348976/field-1/43082b8da21cdc54a702621d76d39594581d5e4d848fd6a50a0a3d4ef85e5bb6" :answer-field/choices ["q-348976/field-1/43082b8da21cdc54a702621d76d39594581d5e4d848fd6a50a0a3d4ef85e5bb6" "q-348976/field-1/9d25723a5db975934b4a4f87336359c9306e6e88d4ce71608f50b86c88284c1b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-348976" :question/id #uuid "90a8232e-fe3a-5d08-9a00-221f3761736e" :question/math-academy-id "q-348976" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{-4}^{0}\\frac{5x-1}{{x}^{2}+4x-5}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We'll work out the indefinite integral first and then proceed with the definite integral.\n\nFirst, we note that the denominator of the integrand can be factored as\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+4x-5=(x+5)(x-1).\n$$\n\nSo the integrand can be converted into a sum of partial fractions,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5x-1}{{x}^{2}+4x-5} & =\\frac{5x-1}{(x+5)(x-1)}=\\frac{A}{x+5}+\\frac{B}{x-1},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n5x-1=A(x-1)+B(x+5).\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=1,$ we can eliminate $A$ and solve for $B:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5(1)-1 & =A(1-1)+B(1+5) \\\\ 4 & =6B \\\\ B & =\\frac{2}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, plugging in $x=-5,$ we can eliminate $B$ and solve for $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5(-5)-1 & =A(-5-1)+B(-5+5) \\\\ -26 & =-6A \\\\ A & =\\frac{13}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{5x-1}{{x}^{2}+4x-5}=\\frac{13}{3(x+5)}+\\frac{2}{3(x-1)}.\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{5x-1}{{x}^{2}+4x-5}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{13}{3(x+5)}+\\frac{2}{3(x-1)})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{13}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+5|+\\frac{2}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-1|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can simplify the result using the laws of logarithms, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{5x-1}{{x}^{2}+4x-5}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{13}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+5|+\\frac{2}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-1|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the definite integral is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-4}^{0}\\frac{5x-1}{{x}^{2}+4x-5}\\,\\text{d}x & ={[\\frac{13}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+5|+\\frac{2}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-1|]}_{-4}^{0} \\\\  & =(\\frac{13}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)+\\frac{2}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1))-(\\frac{13}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1)+\\frac{2}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)) \\\\  & =\\frac{13}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)-\\frac{2}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5) \\\\  & =\\frac{11}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-348976/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "771dfcc1-f6c3-59ed-8961-3fe477b011b6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-348976"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-349040/field-1/b736e872c138ca42210ea0fb910f43996800d08cb768ab6140e866ec6915703c" :answer/id #uuid "3cfb5d8c-8454-5d20-9a85-a0ce83e2d18a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\ln(\\frac{49}{48})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-349040/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "6228426c-c1df-5f2b-b917-c412d67493dc" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-349040/field-1/b736e872c138ca42210ea0fb910f43996800d08cb768ab6140e866ec6915703c" :answer-field/choices ["q-349040/field-1/b736e872c138ca42210ea0fb910f43996800d08cb768ab6140e866ec6915703c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-349040" :question/id #uuid "047f5aca-d84b-5888-b35a-81b77ae7adbc" :question/math-academy-id "q-349040" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\frac{1}{2}}\\frac{36x-10}{12{x}^{2}-x-6}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We'll work out the indefinite integral first and then proceed with the definite integral.\n\nFirst, we note that a denominator of the integrand can be factored as\n\n$$\n12{x}^{2}-x-6=(4x-3)(3x+2).\n$$\n\nSo the integrand can be converted into a sum of partial fractions,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{36x-10}{12{x}^{2}-x-6} & =\\frac{36x-10}{(4x-3)(3x+2)}=\\frac{A}{4x-3}+\\frac{B}{3x+2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n36x-10=A(3x+2)+B(4x-3).\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=\\frac{3}{4},$ we can eliminate $B$ and solve for $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}36(\\frac{3}{4})-10 & =A(3(\\frac{3}{4})+2)+B(4(\\frac{3}{4})-3) \\\\ 17 & =\\frac{17}{4}A \\\\ A & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, plugging in $x=-\\frac{2}{3},$ we can eliminate $A$ and solve for $B:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}36(-\\frac{2}{3})-10 & =A(3(-\\frac{2}{3})+2)+B(4(-\\frac{2}{3})-3) \\\\ -34 & =-\\frac{17}{3}B \\\\ B & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{36x-10}{12{x}^{2}-x-6}=\\frac{4}{4x-3}+\\frac{6}{3x+2}.\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{36x-10}{12{x}^{2}-x-6}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{4}{4x-3}+\\frac{6}{3x+2})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|4x-3|+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|3x+2|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can simplify the result using the laws of logarithms, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{36x-10}{12{x}^{2}-x-6}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|4x-3|+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|3x+2|+C \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|(4x-3)(3x+2)^{2}|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the definite integral is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\frac{1}{2}}\\frac{36x-10}{12{x}^{2}-x-6}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|(4x-3)(3x+2)^{2}|{|}_{0}^{\\frac{1}{2}} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{49}{4})-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(12) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{49}{48}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{49}{48}).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-349040/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "771dfcc1-f6c3-59ed-8961-3fe477b011b6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-349040"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-349041/field-1/ca271a970ed59809d52862bfe2af79764927f79c5be54199cfa45551a2dda235" :answer/id #uuid "e131523c-815a-54eb-8aac-8845ae79f21d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\ln(\\frac{2}{121})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186316415 :answer-field/choices ["q-349041/field-1/ca271a970ed59809d52862bfe2af79764927f79c5be54199cfa45551a2dda235"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-49764/selection/295dac5fa4d5d64455f39d27ce39681f8b19b2c4632faab1abe33e3d767025f0" :answer/id #uuid "0c15b682-54ba-583f-b3a3-0e98a586679c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5\\operatorname{ln}⁡2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49764/selection/f3dac89f2ee5e33877fb0ae412fdefdc0cdcceb7dcdcd6e702e1e3ff0391e011" :answer/id #uuid "93a85711-e1c9-5c86-8690-c53ec526beac" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49764/selection/0781888fd5d22ae2847c5c8ae1fba1203e0c98385e639f0f701e302c7faac595" :answer/id #uuid "b3affa57-2258-54f8-b3f1-f7b03d929bef" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49764/selection/914ea92fc166e257276986674fb61baacfcc748c57d297434376702a0dd8c191" :answer/id #uuid "475f4de0-d7ee-5a39-8286-6799cb3114bc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\operatorname{ln}⁡5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49764/selection/817f30d812e4045140bf7109267d67b609a47bf056f02c6a58b11058515d7583" :answer/id #uuid "2664f4aa-a1dc-51f5-ad32-c5c8d0577db1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49764/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "2469b527-adf4-519b-9594-48dd0849db3e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-49764/selection/817f30d812e4045140bf7109267d67b609a47bf056f02c6a58b11058515d7583" :answer-field/choices ["q-49764/selection/295dac5fa4d5d64455f39d27ce39681f8b19b2c4632faab1abe33e3d767025f0" "q-49764/selection/f3dac89f2ee5e33877fb0ae412fdefdc0cdcceb7dcdcd6e702e1e3ff0391e011" "q-49764/selection/0781888fd5d22ae2847c5c8ae1fba1203e0c98385e639f0f701e302c7faac595" "q-49764/selection/914ea92fc166e257276986674fb61baacfcc748c57d297434376702a0dd8c191" "q-49764/selection/817f30d812e4045140bf7109267d67b609a47bf056f02c6a58b11058515d7583"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-49764" :question/id #uuid "c679d3d1-b950-5f64-a26b-57b3e4e6ca7f" :question/math-academy-id "q-49764" :question/problem "${\\int }_{-6}^{-5}\\frac{5x+29}{(x+7)(x+4)}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "We'll work out the indefinite integral first and then proceed with the definite integral.\n\nFirst, we convert the integrand into a sum of partial fractions:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5x+29}{(x+7)(x+4)}=\\frac{A}{(x+7)}+\\frac{B}{(x+4)},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n5x+29=A(x+4)+B(x+7).\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=-4,$ we can eliminate $A$ and solve for $B:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5(-4)+29 & =A(-4+4)+B(-4+7) \\\\ 9 & =3B \\\\ B & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, plugging in $x=-7,$ we can eliminate $B$ and solve for $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5(-7)+29 & =A(-7+4)+B(-7+7) \\\\ -6 & =-3A \\\\ A & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{5x+29}{(x+7)(x+4)}=\\frac{2}{(x+7)}+\\frac{3}{(x+4)}.\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{5x+29}{(x+7)(x+4)}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{2}{x+7}+\\frac{3}{x+4})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\int \\frac{1}{x+7}\\,\\text{d}x+3\\int \\frac{1}{x+4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+7|+3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+4|+C \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|(x+7)^{2}|+\\operatorname{ln}⁡|(x+4)^{3}|+C \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|(x+7)^{2}(x+4)^{3}|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can simplify the result using the laws of logarithms, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{5x+29}{(x+7)(x+4)}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|(x+7)^{2}|+\\operatorname{ln}⁡|(x+4)^{3}|+C \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|(x+7)^{2}(x+4)^{3}|+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the definite integral is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-6}^{-5}\\frac{5x+29}{(x+7)(x+4)}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|(x+7)^{2}(x+4)^{3}|{|}_{-6}^{-5} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({2}^{2})-\\operatorname{ln}⁡({2}^{3}) \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-3\\operatorname{ln}⁡2 \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-49764/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "771dfcc1-f6c3-59ed-8961-3fe477b011b6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-49764"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-49769/selection/2f3f30a9763db6222fe2895e47cfda47777fa2b71fdb0dadcd325489da7e3ed8" :answer/id #uuid "dc693f8f-4f80-5de6-b23a-c6e99a4d8224" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49769/selection/a7b50e91c4359e8af2412ddd4451ddf4728e6291cb21cd54b2a36f8d20bcfc13" :answer/id #uuid "fe5fd2cc-2907-5150-b596-3ae683c6b16b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49769/selection/9ae9c6442a05750f18b4775d39906961f3bf4d4a05abe08674a042afbad8b2ab" :answer/id #uuid "11efaf85-1aef-5f48-b369-35549de3bc38" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49769/selection/e58f9cbeeaf7149aea3dc0304ce1ab5dd08366ab05046a29fe1788abd26bce29" :answer/id #uuid "bb83e933-4eb8-5113-b1d3-b32068ecb7d2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5\\operatorname{ln}⁡3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49769/selection/0eef758186e17eb7a5ee456810146e51542b13106810829634d974baad29ace4" :answer/id #uuid "562475c1-e434-5753-8042-2c41d767c445" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49769/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "3c228321-9111-5d70-9524-860262e81cab" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-49769/selection/2f3f30a9763db6222fe2895e47cfda47777fa2b71fdb0dadcd325489da7e3ed8" :answer-field/choices ["q-49769/selection/2f3f30a9763db6222fe2895e47cfda47777fa2b71fdb0dadcd325489da7e3ed8" "q-49769/selection/a7b50e91c4359e8af2412ddd4451ddf4728e6291cb21cd54b2a36f8d20bcfc13" "q-49769/selection/9ae9c6442a05750f18b4775d39906961f3bf4d4a05abe08674a042afbad8b2ab" "q-49769/selection/e58f9cbeeaf7149aea3dc0304ce1ab5dd08366ab05046a29fe1788abd26bce29" "q-49769/selection/0eef758186e17eb7a5ee456810146e51542b13106810829634d974baad29ace4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-49769" :question/id #uuid "9186ef7b-f943-5612-ab7d-546d5deb9817" :question/math-academy-id "q-49769" :question/problem "Evaluate ${\\int }_{-2}^{-1}\\frac{x+1}{x(x+3)}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "We'll work out the indefinite integral first and then proceed with the definite integral.\n\nFirst, we convert the integrand into a sum of partial fractions:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x+1}{x(x+3)} & =\\frac{A}{x}+\\frac{B}{x+3},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives\n\n$$\nx+1=A(x+3)+Bx.\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=-3,$ we can eliminate $A$ and solve for $B:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3+1 & =A(-3+3)+B(-3) \\\\ -2 & =-3B \\\\ B & =\\frac{2}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, plugging in $x=0,$ we can eliminate $B$ and solve for $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0+1 & =A(0+3)+B(0) \\\\ 1 & =3A \\\\ A & =\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{x+1}{x(x+3)}=\\frac{1}{3x}+\\frac{2}{3(x+3)}.\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{x+1}{x(x+3)}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{1}{3x}+\\frac{2}{3(x+3)})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x+\\frac{2}{3}\\int \\frac{1}{x+3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+\\frac{2}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+3|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can simplify the result using the laws of logarithms, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{x+1}{x(x+3)}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+\\frac{2}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+3|+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x(x+3)^{2}|+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the definite integral is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-2}^{-1}\\frac{x+1}{x(x+3)}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x(x+3)^{2}|{|}_{-2}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡4-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{4}{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-49769/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "771dfcc1-f6c3-59ed-8961-3fe477b011b6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-49769"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
